CANDIDATE — NOT APPLIED. Trade-off decision for Austin (2026-08-28 10:15).

Marks the DFlash-2 drafter's sliding-window KV group inert for CPU offloading,
reusing the machinery already in place for the kpool tail group.

Effect (from patches/cstech-offload/kv_offload_dryrun.py, `--no-drafter` row
is the exact post-patch shape for the offload pool):
  RAM per 60k prompt   146 chunks / 7.39 GiB  ->  80 chunks / 4.05 GiB  (1.82x)
  store per 53,760 tok      4.205 GB          ->  3.104 GB
  RAM-hit load              1.023 GB          ->  0.968 GB
Cost: after an offload (RAM) hit the drafter's sliding window holds stale KV,
so draft acceptance collapses to ~1.0/step until ~2048 tokens have been
generated. Model OUTPUT is unaffected (rejection sampling preserves the target
distribution), and GPU prefix-cache hits are unaffected. Apply only if Austin
prefers reuse depth over post-hit draft acceptance; raising GLM_KV_OFFLOAD_GIB
buys the same depth with no acceptance cost.

